/*
 * File: ormeq_icon.rc
 *
 * The application icon, for the SDL3 build.
 *
 * Two things want it and they want it under this exact name. Explorer and the
 * taskbar take the first icon group in the executable's resources, whatever it
 * is called; SDL asks for it by name -- SDL_RegisterApp() does
 * LoadIcon(instance, "IDI_ICON1") -- and puts what it finds in the window's
 * title bar and in alt-tab. One resource, both jobs.
 *
 * The win32 build has its own resource file (ormeq.rc) because it carries the
 * menus as well, and its icon has to be called ANGBAND: main-win.c uses one
 * string for the window class, the menu, the bitmap and the icon, and that
 * string is a registration key the operating system matches on rather than a
 * word about the game.
 *
 * The icon itself is generated: tools/make_icon.py, where the mark is a block
 * of text rather than a binary nobody can edit.
 */

IDI_ICON1 ICON "ormeq.ico"
